    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "I've fixed the bug! The issue was in `src/money.js` line 13. When converting a decimal price like \"39.95\" to cents, the old code used `.toFixed(2) * 100`, which resulted in floating-point precision errors (3995.0000000000005).\n\nThe fix was simple: use `Math.round()` to ensure the result is always a whole number:\n\n```javascript\n// Before:\nreturn Number(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')).toFixed(2)) * 100;\n\n// After:\nreturn Math.round(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')) * 100);\n```\n\nI tested it and confirmed it now works with 39.95, 12.99, and 10.99. To commit this fix, run:\n\n```bash\ngit add src/money.js\ngit commit -m \"fix: round price to cents to avoid floating-point precision errors\"\n```",
